`verilator_config
// Common lint waivers, passed by every Verilator lint run in this repo. They waive WIDTHEXPAND
// on the operands of + and -, and on the operand of a unary minus, such as a negated literal
// (-5'sd8), and nothing else (SV guide, section 5): compares, port connections and every
// WIDTHTRUNC are still reported. A change here is reviewed like a change to the guide.
// Design-specific waivers go in their own files, passed only for that design (SV guide, section 8).

lint_off -rule WIDTHEXPAND -file "*" -match "*Operator ADD expects*"
lint_off -rule WIDTHEXPAND -file "*" -match "*Operator SUB expects*"
lint_off -rule WIDTHEXPAND -file "*" -match "*Operator NEGATE expects*"
